---
---
<div class="diagram-wrap">
  <p class="diagram-label">Data vs. Interpretation</p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="col-header col-left-header">Generic year-in-review</div>
    <div class="col-divider"></div>
    <div class="col-header col-right-header">Spotify Wrapped</div>

    <div class="row-left">You watched 847 videos.</div>
    <div class="row-arrow">→</div>
    <div class="row-right">You went deep on indie finds.</div>

    <div class="row-left">Your top category: Productivity.</div>
    <div class="row-arrow">→</div>
    <div class="row-right">You're a growth seeker.</div>

    <div class="row-left last">You listened to 50,000 minutes.</div>
    <div class="row-arrow last">→</div>
    <div class="row-right last">You're in the top 1% of listeners.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="bottom-note">
    Same data. Different framing. The interpretation layer is where the value lives.
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .diagram-wrap {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 32px 28px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-border);
    margin: 2rem 0;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  }
  .diagram-label {
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .comparison-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 28px 1fr;
    gap: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .col-header {
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    font-weight: 500;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .col-left-header {
    background: var(--color-background);
    color: var(--color-secondary);
  }
  .col-right-header {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }
  .col-divider {
    background: var(--color-border);
    width: 1px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .row-left {
    background: var(--color-background);
    padding: 14px 16px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    line-height: 1.4;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .row-arrow {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .row-right {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    padding: 14px 16px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    line-height: 1.4;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-blue);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .row-left.last,
  .row-arrow.last,
  .row-right.last {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .bottom-note {
    margin-top: 20px;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .comparison-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .col-divider {
      display: none;
    }
    .row-arrow {
      display: none;
    }
    .row-right {
      border-top: none;
    }
  }
</style>
